{"skill":{"slug":"log-analyzer","displayName":"Log Analyzer"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770155086063,"changelog":"Initial release: Log parsing, error pattern analysis, stack trace extraction, JSON structured logging, real-time monitoring, multi-service correlation","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":14799,"sha256":"4904a11154b6989befe79d5a1ffe949a76788955395a61d62106d28187928bc5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2131,"sha256":"8a88199c002478d4ffbd459b537354f673e33a9259d32215f3e81863c0c85013","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031420955,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f2ccaa4cfaa6cfe85f04175cee459c4525fcbb343776bfeccc7e759c6675575a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f2ccaa4cfaa6cfe85f04175cee459c4525fcbb343776bfeccc7e759c6675575a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: log-analyzer\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides a comprehensive set of tools and instructions for log analysis, including parsing, searching, and reporting on various log formats. All commands and embedded scripts (Bash and Python) operate on local log files using standard system utilities (`grep`, `awk`, `jq`, `python3`, `tail`, `sort`, `zgrep`, `shuf`, `sed`, `date`, `wc`). There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the agent's purpose. All operations are directly aligned with the stated goal of log analysis.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161173601},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":13,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789031420955},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward log analysis guide, but users should handle logs as sensitive data and pin example dependencies in real projects.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Reading /var/log paths and production-style logs is proportionate for debugging, but logs may contain personal data, tokens, or operational secrets.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a Markdown-only skill with no install scripts, but it includes example npm and pip install comments without pinned versions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Examples search local log files and extract fields such as user IDs, request IDs, messages, and IPs, which is expected for log analysis but should be scoped to authorized logs.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, background service, tool hijacking, memory writing, or hidden execution behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's purpose is to parse, search, monitor, and summarize application logs; the commands and examples fit that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install is reasonable for log debugging workflows. Use it only on logs you are authorized to inspect, avoid printing or sharing sensitive fields, redact personal data and secrets before exporting results, and pin dependency versions when adapting the structured logging examples.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The cited jq examples do extract userId and message fields from logs; this is purpose-aligned, but the artifact would benefit from an explicit privacy and redaction warning.\n[SQP-2] expected: The structured logging examples include userId, user_id, and IP fields; these are common logging examples, but users should minimize and sanitize sensitive fields.\n[T08] expected: The pino and structlog install lines are example comments rather than a skill install mechanism; pinning versions remains advisable for real projects.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031420955}}}}}